diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index b2f4b39..d790b1a 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,15 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+- Fix main-thread stack overflows in debug builds (lurq#25, lurq#26). An unoptimized build gives every temporary its own stack slot, and lurq rebuilds dirty components inside the input event, so a whole-window rebuild ran on the event's stack with several copies of every element per component level. Kontur's desktop overflowed the 1 MiB Windows main-thread stack on its first click on 0.22.1 (1,006,584 bytes on a path that took 767,336 on 0.20.0). The new `stack_depth` regression test (an editor-sized screen under `WindowChrome`, ten nested component levels, laid out, painted and re-rendered from a key event on a 1 MiB thread) needed 1104 KiB on 0.22.1 and needs 208 KiB now; the build and rebuild part alone needs 144 KiB. `scripts/stack-depth-probe.py` measures the smallest stack it passes on.
+  - `Element` holds its root node on the heap and is now 8 bytes instead of 3616. Component builders already boxed their node, so converting one into an `Element` moves a pointer. `WindowChrome` shrinks from 19,112 to 872 bytes and `ChromeTitleBar` from 15,368 to 760; `Modal` and `Overlay` also box their content.
+  - A node's hover, active and focus styles and its event handlers are allocated on first use. A node is 1240 bytes with default features (was 3640) and 1552 with all features.
+  - `Ctx::mount`, dirty-subtree refresh, retained-node cloning, overlay indexing and quad collection keep node-sized temporaries out of their recursive frames. Quad collection used 20.8 KB of stack per tree level and now uses 2 KB.
+  - A size-budget test (`src/size_budget.rs`) fails the test build when the role enums, `Element`, `Node`, `WindowChrome` or `ChromeTitleBar` outgrow their budgets.
+- Shrink `SpacingSize`, `RadiusSize`, `BorderSize` and `TypographyStyle` from 24 to 8 bytes (lurq#26). Their `Extra` variants carry a `RoleName`, a 4-byte handle to the interned name, instead of a `&'static str`. `RoleName` dereferences to `str`, compares equal to `&str`, prints as the name, and converts from `&str`, `String` and `Arc<str>`. `extra(name)`, the `From<&str>`/`From<Arc<str>>` conversions, the theme tables and the `Theme` setters are unchanged.
+- Breaking: `SpacingSize::Extra("name")` (and the same for the other three roles) no longer compiles; use `SpacingSize::extra("name")` or `Extra(RoleName::new("name"))`. A matched `Extra(name)` binds a `RoleName`; call `name.as_str()` where a `&'static str` is needed. `as_str()` on these four roles is no longer `const fn`.
+
 ## 0.22.2 — 2026-09-24
 
 - Fix contexts provided in `create` disappearing when an ancestor re-rendered. Reusing a child replaced its whole context map with the parent's, dropping the values the child had provided, so descendants got `None` from `use_context` and lost `consume_context` subscriptions. A component's `create`-time values now persist for its lifetime, layered over the inherited contexts whenever those change. A value provided during `render` belongs to that render: it is dropped when a later render does not provide it again (it used to linger until the parent re-rendered). Providers whose inherited contexts did not change are no longer re-rendered, with their subtree, on every parent re-render. The `QueryClient`-only workaround for this is removed. The Ctx and Reactivity guides describe the lifetime rules.
